# Colophon

How this capsule is made.

## Hosting

This capsule lives on tilde.pink, a Gemini-only tilde server in the tildeverse, a loose collective of public Unix servers you can get a free home on. The files here are plain text written in Gemtext, served on port 1965.

=> gemini://tilde.pink/ tilde.pink
=> https://tildeverse.org/ The Tildeverse

## Writing & Tools

Posts are drafted in Markdown in Micro and Gram, and converted to Gemtext with a little tool I built, and then synced up to the tilde over ssh and rsync.

=> https://gemtext.brennan.day My Markdown-to-Gemtext converter
=> https://micro-editor.github.io Micro, a friendly terminal editor
=> https://gram-editor.com/ Gram, a GUI code editor for humanoid apes and grumpy toads

## Design

Gemini doesn't allow CSS, JavaScript, images, or layout. Your client decides how everything looks, from fonts to colours. The only "design" here is the ASCII art and the words themselves.

That means no cookies, no tracking, no analytics, no ads. I have no idea how many people read this, and I like it that way.

